{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The events’ Swift types are the source of their schema. A tracking plan, the JSON Schema (draft"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2020-12) of every event an app tracks, is exported from them for the people and tools outside the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app. "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its own that "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves out) turns schemas into the plan’s files, one document per event and an index, as values:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import TrackingPlans","","let plan = TrackingPlan(schemas: [CheckoutStarted.schema])","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", \"checkout_started.v2.schema.json\", \"checkout_started.v2.example.json\"]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The bytes depend on the schemas alone: keys sorted, two-space indentation, a trailing newline and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no timestamps, the same on every run and platform, so the plan can be committed and reviewed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-each-document-says","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What each document says"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each document requires the properties that are neither optional nor have a default value, allows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the optional ones, and rejects any other property. It carries the event’s version and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consent category ("},{"code":"x-traffluent-version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"x-traffluent-consent-category","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). A "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property is marked "},{"code":"x-traffluent-sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and one with a default value is marked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"x-traffluent-default","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and isn’t required, since an earlier release’s payload lacks it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A property removed at the same version stays in the document with the schema it had, marked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"deprecated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and not required, so the payloads of releases that still send it validate: exporting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over the committed plan carries it forward. ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s documentation lists how each Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type maps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Beside each document is the event’s example, a conformance vector: the payload with every property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set to a fixed value its schema accepts (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"example\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", 0, ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one array element). Another","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platform’s client can encode the same event and compare it against the example.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Exporting-the-plan","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Exporting the plan"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tool can only read the schemas of types it is compiled against, so the plan is written by a small"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executable in your package that lists your events:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Package.swift",".executableTarget(name: \"AppTrackingPlan\", dependencies: [","    \"AppEvents\",","    .product(name: \"TrackingPlans\", package: \"Traffluent\"),","]),"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The example package’s executable, ","type":"text"},{"code":"StoreTrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is one:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import StoreEvents","import TrackingPlans","","\/\/\/ Writes the store's tracking plan: `swift package --allow-writing-to-package-directory","\/\/\/ export-tracking-plan`, from Examples\/, writes it into Examples\/TrackingPlan.","@main","struct StoreTrackingPlan: TrackingPlanCommand {","    static let trackingPlan = TrackingPlan(schemas: [","        CheckoutStarted.schema,","        OrderCompleted.schema,","        SignedUp.schema,","    ])","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Then one command, run from the package’s directory, builds it and writes the plan into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["swift package --allow-writing-to-package-directory export-tracking-plan"],"syntax":"sh"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"export-tracking-plan"},{"text":" plugin runs the package’s one executable target that depends on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--product <name>"},{"text":" picks one of several, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--output <directory>"},{"text":" writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elsewhere in the package. Writing again deletes the documents of events the plan no longer lists.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the plan ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StoreTrackingPlan"},{"text":" writes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Checking-the-plan","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Checking the plan"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The committed plan is the contract every platform that sends the events agrees on. One command","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails when the Swift events no longer match it, with a line naming each event and property that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["swift package check-tracking-plan"],"syntax":"sh"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A difference is breaking when, at the same version, a record a store still holds or a payload an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already released app sends may stop decoding or validating:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a removed or renamed event;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a retyped property;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"an optional property made required;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a new required property without a default value;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a default value removed;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a deprecated property declared again with another type, or as required."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anything else leaves the committed plan out of date, which fails with its own message telling you to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"export it again: a new event, a new optional property or one with a default value, a removed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property, a deprecated one declared again as it was, or a changed consent category."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A constraint is compared keyword by keyword. Tightening one is breaking: a higher ","type":"text"},{"code":"minLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a lower ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a new bound, a new or changed ","type":"text"},{"code":"pattern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Loosening one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only leaves the plan out of date. An integer type narrowed to one of fewer bits tightens its bounds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same way. Raising an event’s version (","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event(version: 3)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is how a breaking change is made on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"purpose: the new version gets a document of its own. ","type":"text"},{"code":"--plan <directory>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" checks a plan committed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elsewhere, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--product <name>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" picks the executable, as it does for export.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Checking-from-a-test","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Checking from a test"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same check runs from a test, so it runs wherever the app’s tests do. Add the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" product to a test target that depends on the executable, as the example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"package’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StoreTrackingPlanTests"},{"type":"text","text":" does:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","@testable import StoreTrackingPlan","import Testing","import TrackingPlanTesting","","@Suite(\"StoreTrackingPlan\")","struct StoreTrackingPlanTests {","    @Test(\"The store's events match its committed tracking plan\")","    func eventsMatchTheTrackingPlan() {","        let plan = URL(fileURLWithPath: #filePath)","            .deletingLastPathComponent().deletingLastPathComponent().deletingLastPathComponent()","            .appendingPathComponent(\"TrackingPlan\")","        expectTrackingPlan(StoreTrackingPlan.trackingPlan, matches: plan)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It records an issue with the report the command prints. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan.check(against:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same comparison as a value, each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanDifference"},{"type":"text","text":" with whether it "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isBreaking"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"]}],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","title":"Sampling Events"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","role":"collection","title":"TrackingPlanTesting","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","title":"Consent Gating"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","role":"article","title":"Defining Events","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"},"https://github.com/Tyler-Keith-Thompson/Traffluent/tree/main/Examples/TrackingPlan":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan","title":"Examples\/TrackingPlan","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/tree\/main\/Examples\/TrackingPlan","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Examples\/TrackingPlan"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","title":"Traffluent"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","role":"collection","title":"TrackingPlans","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","title":"Persisting Records"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article","title":"Automatic Tracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"}}}